    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17093" root="روغ" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِيَاغٌ</span></b>  [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِوَاغٌ</span>] <i>A state of plenty;</i> or <i>of
abundance of herbage,</i> or <i>of the goods</i> or <i>conveniences</i> or <i>comforts of life.</i> (JK, Ibn-'Abbád, K.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ فِى الرِّيَاغِ</span> <i>Such a one is in a state
of plenty,</i> &amp;c. (JK.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ريغ</span>.

